// Ore processing (epic #684): the recovery figures every station and machine reads
// (Ore/Core/OreRecovery.cs; README.md "Ore processing"). All of them are starting values for
// playtesting, not settled balance.
//
// Recovery belongs to the machine that did the work (#765); there are no tiers. A fraction is of the
// ore's metal units (raw ore's grade units, which crushed and ground ore and roasted rock carry
// unchanged, one item to one, #847; concentrate holds concentrateUnits), and output carries its
// fraction over from one item to the next (UnitCarry.cs), so nothing is lost to rounding.
//
// - handStations: the hand stations' figures. pan and rocker: concentration (the gold pan 45 %,
//   the rocker 55 %), of the catchable units, × the ore's density; hand stations do not chain.
//   amalgampan: the share of the catchable free gold or silver caught as amalgam, the rest on to
//   the rocker amalgamated. firepit: its roast. cupel and liquationpan: their parting.
// - unclassified, fineUnground, freeUnamalgamated: the locked shares, applied once, at the first
//   concentrator: the share of the feed gravity can catch at all if it skipped classifying (the
//   battery's or ball mill's screen, the riddle), if it is poor ore not ground (the arrastra, the
//   ball mill), if it is free gold or silver not amalgamated (the plates, the amalgam pan). The
//   rest leaves at the table as middlings, or with the last machine's tailings.
// - machines: per machine. recovery: a concentrator's r (sluice, jig, table, vanner; each works on
//   what the one before it missed, 1 - (1 - r1)(1 - r2)..., and nothing on its own kind's
//   tailings), the plates' catch of free metal as amalgam, a roaster's or parting machine's share,
//   1 for a machine that loses nothing. The last step of an ore's ideal route recovers all that is
//   left (the code's FinalStep). load / emptyLoad: resistance working and empty (0.1 a period
//   horsepower; the empty figure a fifth; constant once assembled, except the jaw breaker, the
//   reverberatory and the Parkes kettle, whose load follows the job). water: litres an item from
//   its own reservoir (a rock; a concentrate for the reverberatory; a unit of metal for the acid
//   parting vessel). perHour: items an in-game hour at the reference speed 0.6 (57 shaft turns an
//   hour), in proportion to shaft speed (rock; concentrate for the reverberatory; units for the
//   parting machines). charge / chargeHours: a batch machine's charge (items; units for the Parkes
//   kettle) and its hours at 0.6. zincReturn: the Parkes kettle's zinc back. sulfur: a roaster's share
//   of a sulfide's sulfur it recovers as sulfur powder (the stall roaster's from its heap's crust a third,
//   the reverberatory's 0.7; the firepit none, #765, #925). Scale: 1 t/d of rock
//   = 0.4 rock an hour, of concentrate 3.2 an hour, of metal 16 units an hour (#765).
// - smeltByGrade: what share of its units rock gives in a furnace, by its grade (#847): raw, crushed
//   and ground ore alike, since the furnace slags the rock off and loses metal with it. A sulfide's
//   rock does not smelt until roasted; its roasted rock smelts at this share times its roaster's
//   (the firepit's or the stall roaster's). Those two rules are in the code, not here.
// - smelt: what share of its units each form that is not rock gives in a furnace; a sulfide's
//   concentrate only once roasted (in the code).
// - ores: per ore (the ore part of its code). "class": oxide, sulfide, native, placer (default
//   oxide); "density" (default 1) multiplies concentration; "free": gold or silver that wants
//   amalgamation; "unparted": the share of the main metal a smelt gives without parting (gold
//   quartz 0.85, default 1); "byProducts": a second metal as a share of the main metal's recovered
//   units, won only at a parting step. Unparted, a by-product is lost. Ores not listed are oxides at
//   density 1. "sulfur": a sulfide's sulfur, units per unit of its main metal, from its formula (galena
//   PbS 0.155, chalcopyrite CuFeS2 1.01, pyrite FeS2 1.15; sperrylite, an arsenide, none);
//   sulfurUnitsPerPowder: the units of sulfur in one sulfur powder (5), what a roaster's sulfur comes
//   out as. Argentiferous galena (galena_nativesilver) is a lead ore whose silver share is the
//   silver-rich galena's (#690): galena 3 %, argentiferous galena 38 %. Silver galena was 4.6 % of
//   galena blocks in the survey of #445 and all silver, so 0.954 x 3 % + 0.046 x 38 % = 4.6 % of
//   galena's metal keeps the world's silver.
// - cupel: the bone-ash cupel at the forge (#722; README "Cupellation"). capacityUnits: the most
//   metal units a charge holds (ore and lead added); leadPerOreUnit: lead units a charge needs per
//   unit of an ore whose main metal is not lead (tetrahedrite, freibergite); meltingPoint: the heat
//   (°C) the forge must hold the cupel at; secondsPerIngot: the time per 100 units of charge with the
//   blast gate open (divided by the gate's air: half 0.85, quarter 0.7; shut, nothing happens).
// - liquation: the clay liquation pan in a firepit or the forge (#724; README "Liquation").
//   capacityUnits: the most metal units a charge holds; tinPoint: the heat (°C) the tin sweats out at
//   (the pan's melting point); leadPoint: over it, the lead runs with the tin and the charge gives no
//   lead; secondsPerIngot: the time at the tin point per 100 units of charge.
// - retort: the still (the game's boiler with a condenser beside it, #726). "mercury" is the
//   mercury item (a liquid portion, 100 to the litre); "amalgamMercury" the portions the amalgam pan
//   puts into one amalgam (#718), of which the still returns "mercuryReturn" while the gold or silver
//   stays in the boiler as sponge (smelt "sponge"); "cinnabar" the portions one item of each cinnabar
//   form gives; "portionsPerSecond" the pace (at most 10).
